  "title": "Resolve Fragment"
 },
 "description": "Resolves a half-remembered description of a book, film, song, artwork, person, or event that someone knows exists but can't name. Input reads like a memory (\"there's this thing where...\", \"...somebody who...\", \"...a story about...\") rather than a lookup.\n\nMatches this shape:\n- a musician who became famous largely for stopping performing\n- somebody who photographed the same view every day until the changes became the artwork\n- a song everybody knew but nobody could identify\n- a novel where the footnotes slowly become the real story\n\nNot this shape:\n- what is the capital of France\n- who directed Jaws\n- name of french artist cubist painting 1948\n- which company bought Instagram in 2012\n- any well-documented fact or common trivia \u2014 this tool adds a multi-second round trip with no accuracy benefit there, and is not reliably correct on well-known items either\n\nLatency: calls typically take 10\u201320 seconds.\n\nResults are decide-by-eye, not asserted fact: a resolved title with a confidence level, a ranked shortlist of sources to check, or an explicit \"not resolvable\". Low-confidence findings are surfaced for a human to verify, not claimed as settled.\n\nEach result includes a resolution_id that identifies the stored resolution.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "additionalProperties": false,
  "properties": {
   "fragment": {
    "description": "The half-remembered or fragment-shaped query, in the user's own words. Must be at least 5 characters and describe the thing being recalled by premise, plot, relationship, or context.",
    "maxLength": 500,
    "minLength": 5,
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "fragment"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
 "name": "resolve_fragment",
